<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Castruccio Castracani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1281–<a href="/years/1328">1328</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Castruccio Castracani was a Ghibelline condottiero who became lord of Lucca in 1316. He defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> at Altopascio in 1325, took Pistoia and built a large Tuscan state, and Emperor Louis IV made him Duke of Lucca in 1327. His state collapsed after his sudden death in 1328, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niccolo-machiavelli">Machiavelli</a> later wrote an idealised life of him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/castruccio-castracani.jpg" alt="Castruccio Castracani" width="320" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Benozzo Gozzoli · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cappella_dei_magi,_giuliano_de%27_medici.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
